    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GuZtPZqYPPzHRJ3RcejPed)_\n\nFollows #199 and #206.\n\n## What\n\n- **`litdb` source** for `consult-omni` (in `sp-browsing`): shells out to the `litdb` CLI asynchronously (the previous call is killed as you type, 60 s timeout), so the slow first litdb call does not freeze Emacs.\n  - `litdb` runs `litdb fulltext` and is in the default `consult-omni-multi-sources`.\n  - `litdb semantic` runs `litdb vsearch` (loads the model on each call, so it is only a command, `consult-omni-litdb-semantic`).\n  - Results are candidates in the minibuffer; `RET` on one opens its address (OpenAlex/DOI) with `browse-url`, or visits the file. Generic: any record litdb holds (e.g. later from DEVONthink) shows up.\n  - Disabled when the `litdb` program is not on `exec-path`. `b`/`B` in `sp-search-menu`.\n- **No accidental Google**: `RET` on input that is not a result (results not arrived yet) ran `consult-omni-external-search` in the browser. `sp-consult-omni-ignore-new` now only says nothing was opened.\n\nDocs (`sp-browsing.org`, `sp-search.org`), tangled modules and CHANGELOG updated; tangle check agrees for these files.\n\n## Tested\n\nEmacs 29.3 batch with a fake `litdb` script (arguments, template, parsing, DOI/URL/file candidates, callback). Not run: `consult-omni` itself and a real litdb database (no MELPA/litdb in the container). The `litdb` CLI options were read from litdb 2.2.3.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAPSjQsfh8kjySArne)_",
